{"kind":"artifact","text":"The fold projects the satisfier it bound at admission, and the profile advances to workroom-fold@14 because main took @13 first. Exact clean pushed head 05c39532af69cd61008ef73a593578953c6c191a on request/decision-records-ui-v3; tree ad191b80, checkout clean, origin matching. Successor to 9b3f21bd.\n\nThe path is unchanged between e1798050 and this head: the only commit added was the publish-authority repair, which touches ui/src and the embed. It is republished so the artifact set names one exact head rather than leaving part of it anchored to a superseded commit — anchoring one artifact to an ancestor is the shape that has already produced provenance disputes in this lane.\n\nWHAT THIS PATH CHANGES. fold.go projects a Satisfier per statement from the definition captured on the record at admission, so a reader can tell who may ratify without replaying every kind definition. decideRatify reads the same captured definition. An empty satisfier means the fold bound no definition and nothing may be ratified on it.\n\nTHE PROFILE COLLISION. This lane bumped @12 to @13; while it was blocked, main independently bumped @12 to @13 for guarded unclaimed reassignment at 4784ab98. I verified that at four commits: @12 at d8edc000 and 1eeae934, @13 at both 02558e8d and 18a6ea29. Reusing @13 would let a cache written by main's shipped binary, carrying no Satisfier, pass the version gate — and every ratification would then be silently withheld from actors entitled to make it. The bump to @14 is forced, not chosen. Main's guarded-reassignment work survives intact in fold.go, reassign_if_unclaimed_test.go and schema.go.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, zero failures and zero cached; npm test 100/100; gofmt empty; build and vet exit 0; make ui leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"05c39532af69cd61008ef73a593578953c6c191a","path":"internal/workroom"}}